Chapter: LinLaunderList
  cites Foreword chapter Linear

 Probe (closed by LinearOwnership stage 4): stashing the linear param
 in a list literal moves ownership into the container, which is then
 itself linear. list-at hands the container to a plain parameter -
 the boundary rule rejects the positional read (CDX2065).

Section: Definitions

  spend : linear Integer -> Integer
  spend (n) = let xs = [n]
   in list-at xs 0 + list-at xs 0

  opening : Text = show (spend 21)

